    <Placemark>
      <name>Netiv HaGdud (נתיב הגדוד)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Netiv HaGdud (נתיב הגדוד)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 02. Pre-Pottery Neolithic (PPN) (-8300 to -5500 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Water Reservoir</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Jordan Valley</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.2.5 (Pages 47, 48)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (02. Pre-Pottery Neolithic):</b></p>
<p>A settlement established near a freshwater lake (Lake Salibiya), which formed as the Lisan Lake receded, indicating a wetter climate than today.</p>]]></description>
